<!--****************************************************************************
* \file perimmio-intrinsic.cypersonality
* \version 1.0
*
* \brief
* This personality is allocated on the peri[N] MMIO block (peri[N].mmio) and
* controls the peripheral slave-control (SL_CTL) bus-clock gating at start-up.
* A peripheral ("slave") gets its bus clock ungated when it is always-on
* infrastructure (force="true") or when any of its target resources is used in
* the design.
*
* The peripheral -> {SL_CTL bit, force, targets} map is NOT hard coded here: it
* is read from the device database custom data file mmio_groups.cydata (schema
* http://cypress.com/xsd/cymmiogroups_v1), which the Device Configurator loads
* automatically for the selected die:
*
*   &lt;MmioGroups&gt;
*     &lt;MmioGroup key="PERI0_GR1" peri="0" group="1"&gt;
*       &lt;Slave key="HSIOM"   name="HSIOM"   bit="0" force="true"/&gt;
*       &lt;Slave key="SMARTIO" name="SMARTIO" bit="2" targets="ioss[0].port[0].smartio[0];..."/&gt;
*     &lt;/MmioGroup&gt;
*   &lt;/MmioGroups&gt;
*
* Custom data is addressed by KEY, not by position, so every element carries a
* 'key' attribute (see cymmiogroups_v1.xsd). The personality walks the data with
* the documented custom data API (requires cyhwpersonality_v14 / MTB 3.6+):
*   getCustomDataCount("/MmioGroup")            - number of groups
*   getCustomDataKeys("/MmioGroup", i)          - key of the i-th group
*   getCustomData("/MmioGroup[@key=\"K\"]/@group")
*   getCustomDataCount("/MmioGroup[@key=\"K\"]/Slave")
*   getCustomDataKeys("/MmioGroup[@key=\"K\"]/Slave", j)
*   getCustomData("/MmioGroup[@key=\"K\"]/Slave[@key=\"S\"]/@bit")
*
*
********************************************************************************
